      "content": "Regarding the return of artifacts, proponents argue that restitution honors indigenous rights and culture by recognizing that items were historically stolen or taken under coercion. Conversely, supporters of the \"universal museum\" model contend that keeping artifacts in one location facilitates global scientific study and prevents the fragmentation of knowledge essential for academic progress. To help your report, you might also want to consider the movement toward compromises, such as \"decolonizing immobility\" or creating digital access. You should weigh these perspectives carefully against the specific historical context of each collection. Your final policy should clearly state the guidelines for making these difficult decisions.",
